# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Packaging
*.tgz
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.npm/

# Test / coverage
coverage/
.nyc_output/

# Profiling and benchmarking artifacts. `--cpu-prof`/`--heap-prof` write into
# whatever `--cpu-prof-dir` says (the docs use `.prof`), and the scratch
# harnesses/generated-source dumps used while profiling are throwaway by
# design — see docs/design/performance.md ("Profiling the compiled evaluator").
.prof*/
*.cpuprofile
*.heapprofile
*.heapsnapshot
isolate-*.log
.tmp-perf/
.gen*.js

# Design, review and porting documents: working engineering records, not part
# of the published library. `openspec/` is the OpenSpec workflow's own tree
# (proposal / design / tasks / capability specs for the port) and `docs/design/`
# is where ad-hoc design and code-review notes go. Anything a *reader* of the
# library needs stays tracked: README.md, docs/index.md, docs/design/performance.md,
# docs/error-codes.md, docs/reuse-map.md.
openspec/
docs/design/

# GitHub Pages / Jekyll (docs/ is the site source; these are build/local-preview
# artifacts of it)
docs/_site/
docs/.jekyll-cache/
docs/.jekyll-metadata
docs/.bundle/
docs/vendor/
docs/Gemfile.lock

# Editors
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.iml

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
